A||||5||My7Fieros||HELP!!!!! IM SICK OF THIS %&^*!!!!!||||8||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||08-26-2000||10:27 PM||||Jeez its always something!!!! In a nutshell, the Formula Im restoring seems to have yet something else wrong with it now. It seems that after running for a little while (at least long enough for the engine to reach temp. for the fan to kick on), after shutting it off, I hear something running...a humming sound from under the gear shift.<BR>Ive been experiencing a week/dead battery a couple of times (its a new batt. also) after letting the car run for a short while. What I mean is, I have hardly driven the car since Ive had it. Ive been restoring it so I havnt been driving it. But every once in a while Ill drive it around the block for about 15 or 20 minutes to "keep the blood flowing and the parts moving" if you know what I mean. Twice Ive come back the next day only to find the batt so week that it wont start the car. Well tonight it was in the driveway and I started it and let it run for about 15 minutes or so..the fan kicked on a couple of times, ran fine. BUT, when I turned the car off, I could hear a humming sound under the gear shift. I turned the key to the on position, and the fan came on...ok...whatever....turned it off, then back on..same thing....turned it to the on position again, the fan didnt come on, but I heard that noise. I was thinking it might be the fuel pump constantly running. However, when I turn the key to the on postion, I can hear the distinctive "2 second sound" that the fuel pump makes...WTF? <BR>This is the first time Ive ever really noticed it, but I usually dont pay much attention after I turn the car off. Could this be the reason for the battery drain? What is this sound? Am I gonna have to track down EVERY single F-ing wire in this car? Im getting really sick of this, Im never gonna get to paint this thing! These things are really starting to annoy me. HELP!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000001||fiero56||08-26-2000||10:41 PM||||Fuel pump is still running. Check the oil pressure sender, and remove f/p fuse to kill power to the pump and save battery for temporary fix.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||08-26-2000||10:53 PM||||Yep, oil pressure send/switch bad. Had the same thing.||||reg||14
Z||000003||My7Fieros||08-26-2000||11:10 PM||||You guys rule!! In my blind rage I didnt even THINK about pulling the fuse! DUH!!!! You know whats even worse? I pull the fuse on my daily driver every day for theft purposes! DUH again! (putting on my dunce hat). Well after reading your post, I went over to my friends house where the car is at (luckily its just right around the corner)..I still heard the sound. I started the car to make sure it wasnt too late for the batt, car started right up. I then turned off the car and pulled the fuse (still feeling like a dumba$$) and the sound stopped.<BR>Oh yeah, and I know my oil pressure reg. is going south, my oil guage has always acted wierd...sometimes working..sometimes it just gets pegged all the way to the right, so I was gonna replace it anyway. <BR>I didnt know it regulated the fuel pump too though, so I guess Ill change it and that'll solve the prob (?).<BR>Thanx again guys, this forum RULES!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000004||fiero56||08-27-2000||01:19 AM||||The fuel pump is run through a relay. The way the car is wired, is if the fuel pump relay goes bad, oil pressure sender will take over for the bad relay. When the fuel pump continuously runs even with the car off, the oil pressure sender is stuck in the "closed" position, constantly supplying the fuel pump with juice from the battery.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||08-27-2000||02:01 PM||||The FP relay is used only to charge the system durring cranking when there is no oil pressure. The car runs off the oil pressure switch after that.<P>The contacts of both switches are in parrallel. Either the relay or the O.P. switch can do this. Most likely the O.P. switch.||||reg||1
